    label="A LITTLE CONTEXT"
    title="Curious about what makes systems work."
  />
  <div class="about-content">
    <p class="lead">
      The interface is where a product is experienced. I’m especially interested
      in the engineering that makes it dependable.
    </p>
    <p>
      I enjoy tracing a request through the system: the API contract, the data
      model, the authentication boundary, and the work that happens
      asynchronously. I’m building depth in caching, reliability, deployment,
      observability, and performance—one considered decision at a time.
    </p>
    <p>
      I’m a final-year B.Tech Computer Engineering student at VIIT Pune, with a
      9.1/10 CGPA, and have been selected for Infosys Specialist Programmer L1
      through campus placement.
    </p>
    <div class="about-direction">
      <span class="mono">THE DIRECTION</span>
      <span>
        Stronger fundamentals. Better systems. More thoughtful software.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
